{"repo": {"timestamp": 1794526563000, "version": 20002, "name": "KabelWacht", "icon": "icon.png", "address": "https://muelli.github.io/KabelWacht/fdroid/repo", "description": "Personal F-Droid repository that publishes signed KabelWacht releases, built automatically from tagged commits in CI."}, "requests": {"install": [], "uninstall": []}, "apps": [{"allowedAPKSigningKeys": ["8f02760a5c600a686c7ff452521c7a4be9f8ced922cdc7f9fc639b068625c289"], "authorName": "Tobias Mueller", "binaries": "https://github.com/muelli/KabelWacht/releases/download/v%c/kabelwacht-%c.apk", "categories": ["Connectivity", "Security", "VPN & Proxy"], "changelog": "https://github.com/muelli/KabelWacht/releases", "suggestedVersionName": "6", "suggestedVersionCode": "187", "issueTracker": "https://github.com/muelli/KabelWacht/issues", "license": "AGPL-3.0-or-later", "sourceCode": "https://github.com/muelli/KabelWacht", "added": 1794526560000, "packageName": "com.github.muelli.kabelwacht", "lastUpdated": 1794526562000, "localized": {"en-US": {"description": "KabelWacht is a minimal, fully free-software WireGuard\u00ae client for Android.\n\nIt does one thing well: manage WireGuard tunnels and connect.\n\nFeatures:\n\n* Create, list, search, edit and delete WireGuard profiles. A profile that\n  can no longer be read is shown as invalid, so you can remove it.\n* Import a configuration by scanning a QR code or opening a .conf file.\n* Export a tunnel back to a standard wg-quick .conf file, protected by\n  device authentication \u2014 the file contains your private key.\n* One-tap connect/disconnect with a per-tunnel switch.\n* A status notification with live traffic and the last handshake, and the\n  same numbers on the connected tunnel's row. Alerts tell you when a tunnel\n  fails to connect unattended, is stopped by the system or another VPN, or is\n  connected but not answered by its peer. Each kind has its own notification\n  channel, so Android's settings can mute or raise them separately.\n* A tunnel whose endpoint is a hostname (dynamic DNS) recovers by itself when\n  the peer's address changes.\n* Toggle a tunnel from outside the app: launcher shortcuts, a resizable\n  home-screen widget you can point at a particular tunnel, or a Quick\n  Settings tile (long-press it to open the app).\n* Run conditions: let a tunnel connect and disconnect by itself depending\n  on the network \u2014 only on Wi-Fi, every Wi-Fi except the ones you list,\n  only on chosen networks, never on mobile data or while roaming, or on\n  unmetered connections only.\n* Always-on VPN support, including reconnecting after a reboot.\n* A structured editor with Interface and Peer sections, with the complete\n  wg-quick file one tap away. It shows the tunnel's public key too, ready\n  to copy for whoever administers the server.\n* Fully usable with a hardware keyboard \u2014 shortcuts for search, new\n  tunnel and save, and every control reachable by Tab and arrow keys.\n* Userspace WireGuard backend \u2014 no root required.\n\nPrivacy and freedom:\n\n* 100% free and open-source software (AGPL-3.0-or-later).\n* No trackers, no analytics, no advertising.\n* No Google Play Services or other proprietary dependencies.\n* The only network connection made is your own WireGuard tunnel.\n* Location permission is optional and asked for only if you set up Wi-Fi\n  network-name rules, because Android requires it to read Wi-Fi names.\n  Your location is never used or stored.\n* Release builds are reproducible: anyone can rebuild the published APK\n  from source and get the same bytes.\n\nBuilt on the official WireGuard tunnel library and the ZXing QR decoder.\n\nWireGuard is a registered trademark of Jason A. Donenfeld. This project is not\nofficially affiliated with or endorsed by the WireGuard project.\n", "icon": "icon_zzyLzh1Ecmt4ffPiOm_OK1Os0jQ8X5GkJIP8LQnJOh8=.png", "name": "KabelWacht", "phoneScreenshots": ["1.png", "2.png", "3.png", "4.png", "5.png"], "summary": "A simple, free WireGuard VPN client: scan, import, and manage tunnels.", "whatsNew": "A tunnel that is connected but whose peer does not answer now raises an\nalert, instead of failing silently.\n\nA tunnel with a hostname endpoint (dynamic DNS) reconnects by itself when\nthe peer's address changes.\n\nThe alerts are split over three notification channels, so Android's\nsettings can mute or raise each kind on its own.\n\nThe privacy policy menu is gone from the tunnel list.\n"}}}], "packages": {"com.github.muelli.kabelwacht": [{"added": 1794526562000, "apkName": "kabelwacht-189-rc.apk", "hash": "033bc603732aba1983fb81c72ed83a84d1aa863760f1918fac1daab96e4b40f2", "hashType": "sha256", "minSdkVersion": 29, "nativecode": ["arm64-v8a", "armeabi-v7a", "x86", "x86_64"], "packageName": "com.github.muelli.kabelwacht", "sig": "74a947de067164ce2b712ba8b76f2d40", "signer": "8f02760a5c600a686c7ff452521c7a4be9f8ced922cdc7f9fc639b068625c289", "size": 17324558, "targetSdkVersion": 36, "uses-permission": [["android.permission.INTERNET", null], ["android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE", null], ["android.permission.ACCESS_WIFI_STATE", null], ["android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE", null], ["android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_SPECIAL_USE", null], ["android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_LOCATION", null], ["android.permission.RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED", null], ["android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS", null], ["android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION", null], ["android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION", null], ["android.permission.CAMERA", null], ["android.permission.USE_BIOMETRIC", null], ["com.github.muelli.kabelwacht.DYNAMIC_RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED_PERMISSION", null]], "versionCode": 189, "versionName": "189-rc"}, {"added": 1794526561000, "apkName": "kabelwacht-187-rc.apk", "hash": "ab8c8c06e7f7aa1ab75494fd4f149a0f1406efd1ce7ea22d706fcdcc4e450822", "hashType": "sha256", "minSdkVersion": 29, "nativecode": ["arm64-v8a", "armeabi-v7a", "x86", "x86_64"], "packageName": "com.github.muelli.kabelwacht", "sig": "74a947d